auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  # Nocu API

  Two HTTP services share one JWT secret:

  | Service  | Base URL (local)       | Purpose                                   |
  |----------|------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
  | identity | {{identityUrl}}        | register, login, refresh, current user    |
  | core-api | {{coreApiUrl}}         | incidents CRUD, WebSocket event stream    |

  ## Flow

  1. `identity / Register` creates a user (gets the `viewer` role).
  2. `identity / Login` stores `accessToken` and `refreshToken` in the environment.
     Every other request inherits the bearer token from the collection.
  3. `core-api / incidents / Create` needs `operator` or `admin`. Grant it in SQL, then log in again:

     ```sql
     INSERT INTO user_roles (user_id, role_id)
     SELECT u.id, r.id FROM users u, roles r
     WHERE u.email = 'ops@example.com' AND r.name = 'operator';
     ```

  ## Response envelope

  Success: `{ "data": ... , "meta": { "total", "limit", "offset" } }` (meta only on lists).

  Error: `{ "error": { "code": "not_found", "message": "incident not found" } }`

  Codes: `bad_request`, `unauthorized`, `forbidden`, `not_found`, `conflict`, `internal_error`.

  ## WebSocket

  `GET {{coreApiUrl}}/api/v1/ws?token=<accessToken>` upgrades to a WebSocket.
  The server sends `{"type":"hello"}` then one frame per broker event:

  ```json
  { "type": "event", "subject": "incident.created", "payload": { "type": "incident.created", "occurred_at": "...", "source": "core-api", "data": { ...incident } } }
  ```

  Subjects: `incident.created`, `incident.updated`, `incident.deleted`, `incident.sla_breached`,
  `job.heartbeat`, `job.completed`, `job.failed`.
}
